store_snapshot_sha256":"983238fddc77a88ef4ae3d06b50bcfd25a429f497e89c6af4d9477cefca9cad2","text":"- On 2023-09-15, told Calvin (answering whether it's satisfying to see his hard work pay off, on the restoration finished that day — context in ## Car mod workshop (2023-08-11)) that \"It's so satisfying to see this brought back to life,\" especially seeing people's reactions when they see the finished product — \"makes all the hard work worth it\" [S19T9].\n- On 2023-10-04, said he loves being able to transform something old and beat-up into something beautiful, and that it's the small successes that make him feel proud and fulfilled (said to Calvin right after Calvin praised his grease-stained hands — \"Those hands show you worked hard. You put in lots of effort. You should definitely be proud!\" — context in ## Car mod workshop (2023-08-11)) [S21T10].\n- On 2023-10-08, when telling Calvin about his car show and restored/modified car (details in ## Classic cars), said working on cars \"is not just a hobby, it's a passion\" — it's \"like therapy, a way to get away from everyday stress\"; as a kid he'd spend hours in his dad's garage, tinkering with engines — \"it was like my own sanctuary\" (echoing his childhood memories of working on cars with his dad, see above); now he's \"lucky enough to do this as a job, to take something broken and make it into something awesome\" [S22T5].\n- On 2023-10-08, said doing what he loves has been \"my goal since I was a kid\" and it's awesome that he's able to do it; restoring things can be tough but \"the feeling of accomplishment it gives is great\"; Calvin responded that bringing broken things back to life is \"so satisfying,\" that working on cars \"can be a real escape from reality\" (he understands the feeling), and that \"doing what you love for a living, that's the ultimate goal,\" adding \"Keep going with it, it's really inspiring.\" [S22T5][S22T6][S22T7].\n- On 2023-10-23, told Calvin he recently had a good conversation with some neighbors about current events and politics — it was nice to hear different perspectives and share their own; he finds that interacting like that cheers him up and helps him stay informed (conversation flow in the 2023-10-23 entry of ## Relationships; Calvin's response in the Music and Relationships sections of /memories/calvin.md) [S25T7].\n- On 2023-10-23, told Calvin (who asked \"what made you start working on cars?\") that his car passion started when he was ten: he'd been fascinated with how machines work, found an old car in a neighbor's garage, and asked if he could fix it — \"that's when my love for car engineering began!\" — he enjoyed transforming it from broken-down to high-running, and that sense of accomplishment made him hooked, so he's been working on cars ever since (shared a photo of a man working on a car in a garage; comes with his remark that working on a car is his outlet — \"a little oasis of calm\" — where he's \"connecting back with myself\" — see the 2023-10-23 entry of ## Relationships; complements the childhood memories of tinkering with engines in his dad's garage recorded above; Calvin: \"Impressive! That must have taken a lot of skill and determination to bring that car back to life.\", and asked whether it was a classic car and whether Dave still has it or is working on another project — Dave answered in the continuation of the same day's chat, which is not in this excerpt: he restored a car last year (2022, the 2022 restoration, see above) but sold it to a collector, and is now working on a new car project he finds quite a challenge [S25T14][S25T15][S25T16][S25T17].\n- On 2023-10-23, told Calvin (who asked what the toughest part of car restoration is) that it takes a lot of patience but the payoff is worth it, and paying extra attention to detail isn't easy but it pays off — echoing his earlier remarks that small details make his mod project unique and personalized (details in ## Car mod workshop (2023-08-11)) and that the small successes make him proud (see above) [S25T18][S25T19].\n- On 2023-10-25, said working on a car project \"takes me out of my head and calms me down\" — complementing his long-stated \"oasis of calm\"/therapy remarks above [S26T4].","text_sha256":"aa929f0d141fb905c46758df5f81df0ca2af2ae6b6bca26d45a5376af01c78a7","timestamp":null},{"attribution_index_sha256":"98109144a5a23da7a5b89634be2c543ea2366f2abe85f1f3f8a3df64a5e92ce2","attribution_units":[{"dia_ids":["D7:6"],"kind":"curated_fact","line_end":75,"line_start":75,"source_locators":["[S7T6]"],"text_sha256":"cea74ab279d3185be18829ac14563c97a010f22efbcf6efae6badf819fc59039"},{"dia_ids":["D7:7","D7:8"],"kind":"curated_fact","line_end":76,"line_start":76,"source_locators":["[S7T7]","[S7T8]"],"text_sha256":"fd6e971aaac90c1159e73e987e31819af6558b3b1e299984fcd1704d164a632c"},{"dia_ids":["D12:2"],"kind":"curated_fact","line_end":77,"line_start":77,"source_locators":["[S12T2]"],"text_sha256":"5234b159f96aebf277bc12dcbebfd4711d00e72932f09021929f125ecf024ff1"},{"dia_ids":["D17:3","D17:5"],"kind":"curated_fact","line_end":78,"line_start":78,"source_locators":["[S17T3]","[S17T5]"],"text_sha256":"48e799b8598998d6c605c06a4f1d273b66167f24171a5570600b13b9a170013e"},{"dia_ids":["D12:4"],"kind":"curated_fact","line_end":79,"line_start":79,"source_locators":["[S12T4]"],"text_sha256":"0519b9d96df5806838ae4b62667e21fca0021c43ac303b44ca9f05febced9c38"}],"dia_ids":["D7:6","D7:7","D7:8","D12:2","D17:3","D17:5","D12:4"],"evidence_id":"ev-54c644357d1c2ed4e6892c1fb57cae258b527359a75842d42dcd0d61004d5b1c","group_id":"/memories/dave.md > # Dave","line_end":79,"line_start":75,"observation_ids":["obs-0002"],"path":"/memories/dave.md","query_terms":["dad","car","show","neighbor","automotive","engineer","hook"],"rank":5,"records_sha256":"130a5a1e1b75083358ef27a98dd215a4e75c819ace6f2ee9b560ba394e0f0394","retrieval_round":4,"schema_version":1,"score":0.03177805800756621,"section":"# Dave > ## Hobbies and sense of purpose","selection_ordinal":7,"session